  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.0.0: First stable release. The public API and the pqc.v1 token format are FROZEN and follow SemVer — every token minted by a 0.x preview still decrypts. The PostQuantum.KeyManagement dependency moves to its stable 1.0.1, so the whole PostQuantum.* chain is stable. Since the previews, this release adds: whole-file CLI workflows (protect-file / reprotect-file — atomic, idempotent, fail-closed); keyless token inspection (ProtectedTokenInfo.TryInspect and pqc-config inspect — find tokens on a retired key after rotation); hybrid post-quantum CLI workflows on .NET 10+ (keygen, --recipient sealing to a public key, reprotect-file --to-recipient to migrate a whole config file onto ML-KEM-768 + ECDH P-256 wrapping); defensive guardrails (audit: keyless plaintext-secret scan; check: pre-deploy decrypt gate; VerifyAsync: startup self-test); and a fail-closed hardening fix (all unwrap failures now surface as the single opaque ConfigurationProtectionException). 116 tests, zero skips where ML-KEM is available. Honest scope: the default provider is symmetric-by-key-size post-quantum; the hybrid provider adds PQ asymmetric key wrapping but is not a named standard. NOT independently audited — no audit currently scheduled; 1.0 is a stability commitment, not an audit claim. See CHANGELOG.md, KNOWN-GAPS.md, and docs/PQC-MIGRATION.md.",
